# Learning Objectives - Sprint 1.1

## Overview
This document outlines the personal learning goals for Sprint 1.1 across the various modules of the DAW2 curriculum.

## Module Objectives

### M0487 - Development Environments
- Set up a clean git workflow using GitHub Projects (Kanban) and GitHub Issues.
- Justify the chosen IDE and tools for coding, debugging, and version control.
- Implement automated testing routines and continuous integration using GitHub Actions.

### M0612 - Web Development in Client Environment
- Develop interactive and dynamic user interfaces using pure JavaScript.
- Handle frontend DOM manipulations and data presentation efficiently.

### M0613 - Web Development in Server Environment
- Understand client-server communication and dynamic web page generation using pure PHP.
- Implement Object-Oriented Programming (OOP) and Model-View-Controller (MVC) architecture without external frameworks.
- Manage persistent state using sessions (`$_SESSION`) and cookies.
- Connect to MariaDB via PDO using prepared statements to prevent SQL Injection.

### M0614 - Web Application Deployment
- Containerize application services (Web Server and MariaDB SGBD) using Docker and Docker Compose.
- Establish a Continuous Integration (CI) pipeline with GitHub Actions.

### M0615 - Web Interface Design
- Design fully responsive user interfaces suitable for desktop and mobile devices.
- Build styled web components using pure CSS3 without external frameworks.
